import meta::pure::test::pct::*;

'''
The leading `width` characters of a string.

The `width` is a maximum, not a requirement: a string already `width` characters or shorter is
returned unchanged rather than padded or rejected, so this is safe to apply to a whole column of
mixed-length values. A `width` of `0` keeps nothing and gives the empty string.

Note that `width` is a length, not a position — unlike `substring(String[1], Integer[1]):String[1]`,
which takes an index and drops what comes before it. `'hello world'->stringTake(5)` gives `'hello'`,
while `'hello world'->substring(5)` gives `' world'`.

The `width` must not be negative.

**Parameters**
- `str` — the string to take from.
- `width` — the maximum number of characters to keep, zero or greater.

**Returns** the leading `width` characters, or the whole string when it is already that short.

**Examples**
```pure
'hello world'->stringTake(5)    // 'hello'
'hello world'->stringTake(11)   // 'hello world'  -- width equals the length
'abc'->stringTake(10)           // 'abc'          -- longer than the string
'abc'->stringTake(0)            // ''
```

**See also** `stringTakeLast(String[1], Integer[1]):String[1]`,
`substring(String[1], Integer[1]):String[1]`, `length(String[1]):Integer[1]`
'''
function <<PCT.function>> meta::pure::functions::string::stringTake(str:String[1], width:Integer[1]):String[1]
{
    if($width < $str->length(), |$str->substring(0, $width), |$str)
}

'''
The characters at the front are the ones kept, and a `width` equal to the length keeps them all.
'''
function <<PCT.test>> meta::pure::functions::string::tests::stringTake::testStringTake<Z|y>(f:Function<{Function<{->Z[y]}>[1]->Z[y]}>[1]):Boolean[1]
{
    assertEquals('hello', $f->eval(|stringTake('hello world', 5)));
    assertEquals('hello world', $f->eval(|stringTake('hello world', 11)));
}

'''
A `width` beyond the end of the string returns it unchanged rather than raising.
'''
function <<PCT.test>> meta::pure::functions::string::tests::stringTake::testStringTakeWidthLongerThanString<Z|y>(f:Function<{Function<{->Z[y]}>[1]->Z[y]}>[1]):Boolean[1]
{
    assertEquals('abc', $f->eval(|stringTake('abc', 10)));
}

'''
A `width` of `0` is legal and keeps nothing, giving the empty string.
'''
function <<PCT.test>> meta::pure::functions::string::tests::stringTake::testStringTakeWidthZero<Z|y>(f:Function<{Function<{->Z[y]}>[1]->Z[y]}>[1]):Boolean[1]
{
    assertEquals('', $f->eval(|stringTake('abc', 0)));
}

'''
A `width` of `1` keeps a single character, not the whole string.
'''
function <<PCT.test>> meta::pure::functions::string::tests::stringTake::testStringTakeSingleCharacter<Z|y>(f:Function<{Function<{->Z[y]}>[1]->Z[y]}>[1]):Boolean[1]
{
    assertEquals('a', $f->eval(|stringTake('abc', 1)));
}

function <<test.Test>> meta::pure::functions::string::tests::stringTake::testStringTakeEval():Boolean[1]
{
    assertEq('hello', stringTake_String_1__Integer_1__String_1_->eval('hello world', 5));
    assertEq('abc', stringTake_String_1__Integer_1__String_1_->eval('abc', 10));
}
